[
  {
    "timestamp": "0:00",
    "content": "Hi, I'm Sean, and welcome to What's New in Wallet."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "0:11",
    "content": "Since their introduction, passers have become an essential part of how people move through their day."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "0:16",
    "content": "From picking up a morning coffee, to tapping through transit gates, to checking in and boarding a flight,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "0:22",
    "content": "all without ever handing over a physical card."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "0:25",
    "content": "Passers help people move through their world faster, more privately, and more securely."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "0:32",
    "content": "In iOS 27, we're taking passes further than ever."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "0:36",
    "content": "iOS 27 introduces a stunning new pass style called post-generic."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "0:41",
    "content": "Four new barcode types, giving you more flexibility at the point of presentation,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "0:46",
    "content": "and a powerful new way for passes to surface relevant actions right below the pass face."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "0:51",
    "content": "And we're also introducing a brand new suite of developer tools for Mac and server platforms,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "0:59",
    "content": "making it easier than ever to design, personalize, and build great passes."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "1:05",
    "content": "We have a lot to cover, so let's dive straight in with the brand new pass style, post-generic."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "1:11",
    "content": "Post-generic is a great fit for membership cards, loyalty programs, store cards,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "1:18",
    "content": "and anywhere you want bold, colorful artwork to take center stage."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "1:25",
    "content": "The pass face consists of a background image, a primary logo, header fields,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "1:32",
    "content": "primary fields, a footer field, and lastly, a barcode if supplied."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "1:41",
    "content": "To adopt this style, in the pass JSON of your pass bundle,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "1:45",
    "content": "specify the post-generic top-level style key."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "1:49",
    "content": "Then, add your content with the usual pass field structure,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "1:53",
    "content": "and the pass will take care of laying everything out across the pass face."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "1:56",
    "content": "One thing to keep in mind is that the pass face supports a single footer field,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "2:02",
    "content": "so if you include more than one, only the first will be displayed."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "2:07",
    "content": "Post-generic requires iOS 27 or later."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "2:11",
    "content": "To support customers on iOS 26 and earlier,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "2:15",
    "content": "we recommend including the existing generic top-level style key,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "2:19",
    "content": "alongside the post-generic style key in your pass JSON,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "2:23",
    "content": "with relevant fields under each."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "2:24",
    "content": "That way, customers who have not yet made the update to iOS 27"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "2:30",
    "content": "will still be able to add your pass to wallet."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "2:34",
    "content": "Next, in iOS 27, pass is support for new barcode types."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "2:39",
    "content": "EAN 13, Code 39, Codabar, and ITF."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "2:45",
    "content": "These are specified using the existing barcode object"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "2:48",
    "content": "and barcodes array in your pass JSON."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "2:50",
    "content": "For example, to present your barcode in Codabar format,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "2:56",
    "content": "set the format of your barcode to PK Barcode Format Codabar."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "3:03",
    "content": "You can find the full list of format definitions"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "3:05",
    "content": "in the wallet passes documentation."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "3:07",
    "content": "Because previous versions of iOS do not support these new formats,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "3:12",
    "content": "we strongly recommend providing an array of barcodes in priority order."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "3:16",
    "content": "By providing multiple barcodes,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "3:18",
    "content": "you give the system the best chance of rendering a barcode your hardware can scan,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "3:23",
    "content": "regardless of which operating system version your customer is on."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "3:26",
    "content": "If you only provide one of the new barcode types and nothing else,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "3:32",
    "content": "the pass will not render a barcode on iOS 26 and earlier."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "3:36",
    "content": "So we recommend leading with your preferred format"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "3:39",
    "content": "and falling back gracefully."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "3:41",
    "content": "Now, we do recognize that there are some circumstances"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "3:49",
    "content": "where supporting multiple barcode types simply isn't an option."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "3:54",
    "content": "If that's your situation, there are two things that you should do."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "3:58",
    "content": "First, surface the credential ID in a pass field"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "4:01",
    "content": "so it can be entered manually"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "4:02",
    "content": "and make it easy to find."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "4:06",
    "content": "Consider using a primary field or a header field"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "4:08",
    "content": "so it's prominent on the pass face."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "4:12",
    "content": "Second, make sure your frontline staff"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "4:15",
    "content": "are trained for manual entry workflows."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "4:17",
    "content": "A pass that can't be scanned"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "4:19",
    "content": "shouldn't result in a blocked customer."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "4:22",
    "content": "Getting this right can mean the difference"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "4:24",
    "content": "between a seamless experience and a frustrating one."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "4:28",
    "content": "Next, let's talk about featured actions."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "4:31",
    "content": "With the second generation event tickets introduced in iOS 18,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "4:35",
    "content": "you can provide semantic URLs"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "4:37",
    "content": "to expose additional user actions drawn below the pass,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "4:40",
    "content": "such as viewing the event schedule."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "4:43",
    "content": "In iOS 27, there's a new flexible API"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "4:45",
    "content": "that allows you to provide actions for all pass styles."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "4:49",
    "content": "In the top level of your pass JSON,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "4:51",
    "content": "define the featured actions key,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "4:53",
    "content": "which takes an array of action objects."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "4:56",
    "content": "Each action is defined as a unique ID,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "4:58",
    "content": "the action type,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "4:59",
    "content": "and a value,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "5:01",
    "content": "such as a URL."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "5:01",
    "content": "For example,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "5:03",
    "content": "to provide an action to view offers,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "5:06",
    "content": "I set the identifier to a unique ID,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "5:09",
    "content": "the action type to membership benefits,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "5:12",
    "content": "and a URL to navigate the user."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "5:15",
    "content": "Wallet draws this below the pass"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "5:17",
    "content": "with an appropriate colorful icon"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "5:19",
    "content": "and a localized call to action."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "5:22",
    "content": "Each pass can contain up to two featured actions."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "5:28",
    "content": "We recommend providing only the most meaningful"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "5:30",
    "content": "and relevant actions to your customers"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "5:33",
    "content": "and provide your actions in priority order."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "5:37",
    "content": "You can find the full list of supported action types"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "5:40",
    "content": "and their expected values"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "5:41",
    "content": "in the wallet passes documentation."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "5:44",
    "content": "Now,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "5:45",
    "content": "passes have gained a lot of features and functionality"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "5:47",
    "content": "over the last decade,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "5:49",
    "content": "and it can be hard to connect"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "5:50",
    "content": "what is described in the pass bundle"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "5:52",
    "content": "to the visual representation presented on device."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "5:56",
    "content": "So we're excited to announce a brand new app for Mac"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "5:59",
    "content": "that makes designing passes easier than ever,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "6:03",
    "content": "and it's called Pass Designer."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "6:06",
    "content": "Pass Designer is a what you see is what you get editor,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "6:10",
    "content": "giving you a true to iOS rendering of your pass"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "6:13",
    "content": "as you build it."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "6:16",
    "content": "Pass Designer creates template files."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "6:19",
    "content": "To convert a template into a personalized signed pass"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "6:22",
    "content": "ready for distribution,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "6:24",
    "content": "alongside Pass Designer,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "6:26",
    "content": "we're also announcing a new Swift on server package"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "6:29",
    "content": "called Pass Builder."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "6:31",
    "content": "Pass Builder runs on Mac and Linux."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "6:35",
    "content": "It provides a Swift API"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "6:36",
    "content": "and a command line executable called Build Pass."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "6:40",
    "content": "Now,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "6:40",
    "content": "my friend Stacy runs a doggy daycare,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "6:43",
    "content": "and I want to help her create membership cards"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "6:45",
    "content": "for each of her fluffy clients."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "6:48",
    "content": "I'm going to use Pass Designer to design a template"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "6:50",
    "content": "and then use Pass Builder on server"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "6:53",
    "content": "to personalize the template"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "6:54",
    "content": "and distribute passes at scale."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "6:57",
    "content": "Let's jump into Pass Designer."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "6:59",
    "content": "And here we go."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:01",
    "content": "A live preview of the pass on the right"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:04",
    "content": "and a sidebar to edit the pass on the left."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:08",
    "content": "The sidebar allows you to configure"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:10",
    "content": "the pass identity and signing configuration,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:13",
    "content": "the pass style,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:15",
    "content": "images,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:16",
    "content": "barcodes,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:17",
    "content": "fields,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:18",
    "content": "and semantics"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:18",
    "content": "if the pass style supports it."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:20",
    "content": "So this is a bit of a blank canvas,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:23",
    "content": "but I know Stacy takes some gorgeous portrait photos"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:26",
    "content": "of each dog."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:27",
    "content": "So let's experiment"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:28",
    "content": "with the new poster generic style"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:30",
    "content": "and see how those photos look."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:32",
    "content": "So I'm going to go into Style"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:33",
    "content": "and change the pass style"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:36",
    "content": "to poster generic."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:37",
    "content": "And then I'm going to navigate"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:40",
    "content": "to images in the sidebar"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:42",
    "content": "and drag in a sample photo"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:44",
    "content": "Stacy has given me from my desktop."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:48",
    "content": "That looks like it fits quite nicely."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:51",
    "content": "Now let's add some fields."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:54",
    "content": "I'm going to navigate to header fields"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:55",
    "content": "in the sidebar"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:56",
    "content": "and add a new header field."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "7:59",
    "content": "I'm going to set the key to dog ID"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:01",
    "content": "and the label to member ID"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:03",
    "content": "and add a placeholder ID"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:05",
    "content": "to see how it looks."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:08",
    "content": "Great."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:09",
    "content": "Now let's add some primary fields"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:11",
    "content": "for dog name"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:12",
    "content": "and their favorite toy."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:14",
    "content": "In the sidebar,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:16",
    "content": "I'm going to navigate to primary fields"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:17",
    "content": "and add a primary field for name."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:22",
    "content": "I'll set the key to dog name."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:26",
    "content": "Now,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:27",
    "content": "here's a neat trick"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:27",
    "content": "with the poster generic pass face."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:30",
    "content": "If I omit the label"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:31",
    "content": "on the first primary field,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:34",
    "content": "we'll get the cool bold title"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:36",
    "content": "for the field value."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:39",
    "content": "So I'm going to type in"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:40",
    "content": "a placeholder name of Finley"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:42",
    "content": "and add a primary field"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:43",
    "content": "for favorite toy."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:45",
    "content": "So again,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:46",
    "content": "I'll navigate to primary fields"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:48",
    "content": "and add a new field."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:50",
    "content": "I'll set the key to loves,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:55",
    "content": "the label to loves,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:56",
    "content": "and add a placeholder value"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "8:59",
    "content": "of flying disk."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:01",
    "content": "And now,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:02",
    "content": "let's make it super easy"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:03",
    "content": "for Stacey to check each dog"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:05",
    "content": "in and out of daycare"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:06",
    "content": "by encoding their member ID"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:08",
    "content": "as a barcode."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:09",
    "content": "I'm going to head over"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:12",
    "content": "to barcode and NFC"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:14",
    "content": "and write in a placeholder"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:16",
    "content": "barcode message."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:18",
    "content": "This works,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:20",
    "content": "but I don't think I need to use"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:21",
    "content": "that much space for a QR code."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:24",
    "content": "Let's try and narrow barcode type instead,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:27",
    "content": "such as PDF417."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:28",
    "content": "I'm going to click on the format picker"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:32",
    "content": "and select PDF417."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:36",
    "content": "That looks much better."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:38",
    "content": "Now let's add some finishing touches"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:40",
    "content": "by adding a primary logo."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:43",
    "content": "I'll navigate to images"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:44",
    "content": "and drag in the primary logo"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:47",
    "content": "from my desktop."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:51",
    "content": "And adjusting the colors"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:52",
    "content": "by navigating to style"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:54",
    "content": "and setting the label color."
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:56",
    "content": "And the final finishing touch,"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "9:59",
    "content": "adding Stacey's doggy daycare"
  },
  {
    "timestamp": "10:01",
    "content": "to the footer."
  },
  {
